Page 1 North America: -------- begin text --------
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌnɔː(ɹ)θ əˈmɛɹɪkə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-North America.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛɹɪkə|s=5}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[north|North]] [[America]]}}

# {{senseid|en|Q49}}The [[continent]] that is the northern part of the [[Americas]]; that part east of the [[Pacific Ocean]], west of the [[Atlantic Ocean]], north of [[South America]] and south of the [[Arctic Ocean]].
#* {{quote-text|en|date=May 12 1991|chapter=[[w:List of Jeeves and Wooster episodes|Kidnapped!]]|title=w:Jeeves and Wooster|section=Series 2, Episode 5
|passage=''Jeeves:'' Foreign travel often liberates emotions best kept in check, sir. The air of '''North America''' is notoriously stimulating in this regard, as witness the regrettable behavior of its inhabitants in 1776.<br>''B. Wooster:'' Hm? What happened in 1776, Jeeves?<br>''Jeeves:'' I prefer not to dwell on it, if it's convenient to you, sir.}}
# {{lb|en|United States|Canada}} Canada and the United States as a unit to the exclusion of Mexico, Central America, the Caribbean nations, and Greenland; roughly equivalent to [[Northern America]]. Often used to describe [[object]]s in a [[context]] that includes only the US and Canada.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|la|India Nova}}
* {{l|en|Turtle Island}}

====Derived terms====
*{{l|en|British North America}}
* {{l|en|North American}}

