Page 285 Εὐρώπη: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Ευρώπη}}
==Ancient Greek==
{{wikipedia|Europa}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|grc|Εὐρώπᾱ||Doric}}
* {{alter|grc|Εὐρωπίᾱ||poetic}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|grc}}, but either from:
* {{m|grc|εὐρύς}} + {{m|grc|ὤψ}}, literally meaning "wide face" (as a description of the beauty of the mythical [[w:Europa_(consort_of_Zeus)|Europa]]) or "broad eye" (metaphorically meaning something like "as far as the eye can see")
* {{der|grc|sem}} origin; compare also {{m|grc|Ἀσία}}, related to
** {{cog|akk|𒀭𒌓𒋙𒀀|tr=<sup>d</sup>UD.ŠU<sub>2</sub>.A|ts=erebu, erbu|t=direction of the setting sun, occident, west}}
** {{cog|phn|𐤏𐤓𐤁|ts=ʿereb|t=evening}}
** {{cog|he|מַעֲרָב|tr=maʿărāḇ|t=occident, west}}
** {{cog|syc|ܡܥܪܒܐ|tr=maʿrəḇā|t=occident, west}}
** {{cog|ar|غَرْب|t=occident, west}} and {{m|ar|غُرُوب|t=setting of the sun}}
** and specifically {{cog|arc|עֲרוּבְתָּא|tr=ʿărūḇtā|g=f|t=sunset; eve; Sabbath eve; Friday; Venus, Aphrodite}} of which the [[absolute state]] {{m|arc|עֲרוּבָא|tr=ʿărūḇā|g=f}} in the relevant {{bor|grc|sem-nwe|-}} chronolect and isolect would have lacked [[begadkefat|begedkefet]] and the second vowel {{IPAchar|/ɔː/}}
* From a separate {{der|grc|sem}} root related to guarantees and exchanges, found in {{cog|ar|عَرَبُون|t=down payment}}, {{cog|he|בֶּן‑עֲרֻבָּה|tr=ben‑ʿărubbāh|t=hostages}}, {{cog|syc|ܥܪܘܒܐ|tr=ˁārōḇā|t=hostages}}, stemming from mythology in which [[w:Europa_(consort_of_Zeus)|Europa]] is famously abducted; see the story of [[w:Cadmus|Cadmus]], a figure also with Semitic associations, who seeks after his kidnapped sister.

