Page 353 Asia: -------- begin text --------
{{also|asia|asía|Ásia|Asía|Àsia|asĩa|.asia}}
==English==
{{swp}}
{{swp|Asia (mythology)}}
{{swp|67 Asia}}
[[File:LocationAsia.svg|thumb|right|250px|The continent of Asia, by the standard definition delimited by the [[Urals]].]]
[[File:Roman Empire Asia.svg|thumb|250px|The former Roman province of Asia]]
[[File:Location-Asia-UNsubregions.png|thumb|right|250px|The {{w|United Nations Statistics Division|UNSD}} divisions of Asia: Northern Asia (blue), Central Asia (purple), Western Asia (green), Southern Asia (red), Eastern Asia (yellow), Southeastern Asia (orange)]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Asia}}, {{m|enm|Asie}}, from {{der|en|fro|Asie}} and {{der|en|la|Asia}}, from {{der|en|grc|Ᾰ̓σῐ́ᾱ}}, from {{der|en|gmy|𐀀𐀯𐀹𐀊|ts=aswijaː}}, in turn probably from {{der|en|hit|𒀸𒋗𒉿|tr=aš-šu-wa|ts=Aššuwa|t=northwest Anatolia}} of uncertain origin. Potentially from an [[w:Tyrsenian_languages#Aegean_language_family|Aegean language family]] substrate or {{der|en|akk|-}}. Possibly a {{dbt|en|Assuwa|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈeɪ.ʒə/|/ˈeɪ.ʃə/|q2=dated}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈeː.ʃja/|/ˈeɪ.ʃja/|a=InE}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Asia.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-Asia.wav|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʒə|eɪʃə|s=2}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q48}} A [[continent]] located east of [[Europe]] (typically delimited by the [[Urals]]), west of the [[Pacific Ocean]], north of [[Oceania]] and south of the [[Arctic Ocean]].
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1669
|origyear=1665
|author=[[w:Johan Nieuhof|John Nievhoff]]
|translator=w:John Ogilby
|title={{w|An embassy from the East-India Company|An Embassy from the Eaſt-India Company of the United Provinces, to the Grand Tartar Cham Emperour of China}}
|url=https://archive.org/details/McGillLibrary-126081-3026/
|origlang=nl
|publisher=John Macock
|location=London
|OCLC=407084353
|page=4
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/McGillLibrary-126081-3026/page/n15/
|text=All '''''Aſia''''', which the Ancients divide into '''''Aſia''''' the Great and '''''Aſia''''' the Leſs, modern Computors part into five Diviſions, ''Perſia'', the ''Turkiſh'' Empire, ''India'', (to which they caſt in the adjacent Iſles) ''Tartary'', and ''China''.}}
# {{lb|en|Greek mythology}} A daughter of Oceanus and Tethys, the wife of the Titan, [[Iapetus]], and mother of [[Atlas]], [[Prometheus]], [[Epimetheus]] and [[Menoetius]].
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} {{w|67 Asia}}, a main belt [[asteroid]].
# {{given name|en|female|from=place names|usage=modern}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1994|author=w:Blake Nelson|title=Girl: A Novel|publisher=Simon&Schuster|isbn=0671897071|page=81
|passage=And Scott Haskell started going out with this sophomore girl called '''Asia''', who was this rich girl from Weston Heights.}}
# {{place|en|ancient province|r/the [[Roman Empire]]|in modern|c/western [[Turkey]]}}.

