==Assyrian Neo-Aramaic==

===Etymology 1===
{{aii-root|ܐ ܣ ܐ}}
{{inh+|aii|arc|אָסְיָא|tr=ʾāsyā}}, from {{der|aii|akk|𒀀𒍪|ts=asû|tr=A.ZU|t=physician, healer}}, from {{der|aii|sux|𒀀𒍪|ts=azu|tr=A.ZU|t=physician, healer; one who knows fluids}}; also borrowed into {{cog|ar|آسٍ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|aii|[ˈʔɑsːjɑː]|a=Standard}}

====Noun====
{{aii-noun|ܐܵܣܝܵܐ|m-s|f=ܐܵܣܝܼܬ݂ܵܐ|pl=ܐܵܣܝܹ̈ܐ|pl2=ܐܵܣ̈ܲܘܵܬ݂ܵܐ}}

# [[medical]] [[doctor]], [[physician]], [[healer]] {{gloss|one who is trained and licensed to heal the sick or injured}}
#: {{uxa|aii|ܡܩܲܘܡܵܐ ܕܝܵܐܹܐ ܕܐܵܙܹܠ݇ܬ ܚܵܙܹܝܬ ܠܹܗ '''ܐܵܣܝܵܐ''' ܐܸܢ ܗܸܫ ܠܵܐ ܝܘܸܬ ܒܸܪܓ݂ܵܫܵܐ ܨܦܵܝܝܼ.|subst=ܕܝܵܐܹܐ//ܕ-ܝܵܐܹܐ|Maybe you should see the '''doctor''' if you still feel unwell.}}
#* {{RQ:aii:Bible|Luke|5|31|passage=ܥܢܹܐ ܠܹܗ ܝܼܫܘܿܥ ܘܐ݇ܡܝܼܪ ܠܹܗ ܐܸܠܲܝܗܘܿܢ، «ܗܸܢܘܿܢ ܕܝܼܢܵܐ ܒܚܘܼܠܡܵܢܵܐ ܠܵܐ ܝܢܵܐ ܣܢܝܼ̈ܩܹܐ ܥܲܠ '''ܐܵܣܝܵܐ'''، ܐܸܠܵܐ ܗܸܢܘܿܢ ܕܚܸܪܒܵܐ ܡܪ̈ܝܼܥܹܐ ܝܢܵܐ».|subst=ܒܚܘܼܠܡܵܢܵܐ//ܒ-ܚܘܼܠܡܵܢܵܐ,ܕܚܸܪܒܵܐ//ܕ-ܚܸܪܒܵܐ|t=Jesus answered them, “It's not the healthy who need a '''doctor''', but the sick.”}}

=====Inflection=====
{{aii-infl-noun/m|ܐܵܣܝ|ircstr=ܐܵܣܹܐ|sg-3cp=ܐܵܣܝܼ}}

=====Derived terms=====
