|ܐܵܣܝܵܝܵܐ<t:[[medicinal]]>
|ܐܵܣܝܘܼܬ݂ܵܐ<t:[[medicine]], [[medical]] [[science]]>
|ܐܵܣܝܘܼܬ݂ܵܢܵܝܵܐ<t:[[medical]]>
|ܡܐܲܣܝܵܢܵܐ
|ܐܵܣܝܵܐ ܒܲܝܬܵܝܵܐ<t:[[family doctor]]>
|ܐܵܣܝܵܐ ܕܟܹܟܹ̈ܐ<t:[[dentist]]>
|ܐܵܣܝܵܐ ܕܫܲܒ݂ܪܹ̈ܐ<t:[[pediatrician]]>}}

===Etymology 2===
{{lbor|aii|syc|-}}, from {{der|aii|grc|Ἀσία}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|aii|[ʔɑsˈːiːjɑ]|a=Standard}}

====Proper noun====
{{aii-proper-noun|ܐܵܣܝܼܵܐ|f}}

# {{place|aii|continent|located east of Europe, west of the Pacific Ocean, north of Oceania and south of the Arctic Ocean|t=Asia}}
#: {{uxa|aii|ܐܝܼܬ݂ ܐܲܪܒܥܝܼܢ ܘܬܡܵܢܝܵܐ ܐܲܬ݂ܪ̈ܲܘܵܬܵܐ ܓܲܘ '''ܐܵܣܝܼܵܐ''' ܐܸܕܝܘܿܡ.|t=There are forty-eight countries in '''Asia''' today.}}
#: {{uxa|aii|ܐܵܣܝܼܵܐ '''ܝܠܵܗ̇''' ܝܲܒܝܼܫܬܵܐ ܛܵܒ݂ ܪܲܒܬ݂ܵܐ ܥܲܠ ܐܲܪܥܵܐ.|'''Asia''' is the earth’s largest continent.}}
# {{lb|aii|historical}} [[Anatolia]], [[Asia Minor]] {{gloss|province of the Roman Empire located in what is now western Turkey}}
#* {{RQ:aii:Bible|Acts|19|10|passage=ܗܵܕ݂ܹܐ ܓܪܝܼܫ ܠܵܗ̇ ܬܲܪܬܹܝܢ ܫܸܢܹ̈ܐ، ܘܗܵܕܟ݂ܵܐ ܟܠܗܘܿܢ ܝܗܘܼܕ݂ܵܝܹ̈ܐ ܘܝܵܘܢܵܝܹ̈ܐ ܕܒܸܥܡܵܪܵܐ ܝܗ݇ܘܵܘ ܓܲܘ ܐܘܼܚܕܵܢܵܐ ܕ'''ܐܵܣܝܼܵܐ''' ܫܡܝܼܥ ܠܗܘܿܢ ܗܹܡܸܙܡܵܢ ܕܡܵܪܝܵܐ.|subst=ܕܒܸܥܡܵܪܵܐ//ܕ-ܒܸܥܡܵܪܵܐ,ܐܘܼܚܕܵܢܵܐ ܕ//ܐܘܼܚܕܵܢܵܐ ܕ-,ܕܡܵܪܝܵܐ//ܕ-ܡܵܪܝܵܐ|t=And this continued for two years, so that all who dwelt in '''Asia''' heard the word of the Lord, both Jews and Greks}}
# {{lb|aii|Greek God}} A daughter of Oceanus and Tethys, the wife of the Titan, Iapetus, and mother of Atlas, Prometheus, Epimetheus and Menoetius.
# {{lb|aii|astronomy}} {{w|67 Asia}}, a main belt asteroid.

