Page 385 Ἀσία: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Ασία}}

==Ancient Greek==
{{wikipedia|Asia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|grc|Ἀσίη||ion}}

===Etymology===
Compare {{cog|gmy|𐀀𐀯𐀹𐀊}}. There is no current consensus on the origin of the word. It originally applied only to [[Anatolia]], and was later extended to its current definition. Likely an extension from or related to {{der|grc|hit|𒀸𒋗𒉿|tr=aš-šu-wa|ts=Aššuwa|t=northwest Anatolia}} of uncertain origin, but perhaps from:
*A proposed {{w|Tyrsenian languages#Aegean_language_family|Aegean language family}} word ''asis'', meaning “muddy” or “silty”, as reference to the silty eastern shores of the Aegean sea.
* {{der|grc|akk|𒀀𒍮|tr=a-ṣu|t=to go out, to rise}} (compare {{cog|he|יצא|tr=yatsá}}), a reference to the rising sun, hence “land of the sunrise”;<ref>Room, Adrian. ''Place Names of the World'', 2nd ed., McFarland & Co., 2006.</ref> this is however potentially problematic as the Aššuwa league was west not east of the Hittite polity. Compare also {{m|grc|Εὐρώπη}}.
* Alternatively from the same {{noncog|akk|-}}, in the sense of “rising, rising up, to leave, to depart”. The Aššuwa league was formed after initial Hittite incursions into the western peninsula as a coalition to balk advancement; described as a rebellion, an uprising or a breaking away of lands on the fringe of Hittite control. A reconciliation between the two could be found as one sense providing the meaning for western Asia-minor in the Hittite view and the other for the sense of the direction in a general sense by the Akkadian terminology. For the early Greeks both the league and the sunrise coincided in the same direction.

More at [[w:Asia#Etymology|Asia]], {{w|Assuwa}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-IPA|Ἀ˘σί˘ᾱ}}
or
{{grc-IPA|Ἀ¯σί˘ᾱ}}
The first vowel is short in prose and long in verse.

===Proper noun===
{{grc-proper noun|Ᾰ̓σῐ́ᾱ|Ᾰ̓σῐ́ᾱς|f|first}}

# {{place|grc|ancient region|r/Western Asia|, approximately covering the area of modern <<c/Turkey>>|t=Anatolia|t2=Asia Minor}}
# {{place|grc|Roman province|in western|r/Anatolia|t=Asia}}

