==Ancient Greek==
{{wikipedia|Libya (mythology)}}
{{wikipedia|Ancient Libya}}

===Etymology===
{{wikipedia|Libu}}
Homeric toponym (Odyssey IX.95, XXIII.311).

From {{af|grc|Λῐ́βῠς|-η}}, from the name of the {{m|en|Libu}}, a tribal people of North Africa, attested in Egyptian inscriptions of the 13th century BC as {{m|egy|rbw}} <hiero>r-b-w-T14-N25</hiero> and as {{m|xpu|𐤋𐤁𐤉}} in later Punic inscriptions.

