[[File:Libya (centered orthographic projection).svg|thumb|right|Libya]]
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Via {{uder|en|la|Libya}}, from {{uder|en|grc|Λιβύη}}. English since the 16th century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lĭbʹē-ə}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈlɪbi.ə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Soundguys-Libya.wav|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-Libya.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|Lib|ya}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪbiə|s=3}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q1016}}{{place|en|country|r/North Africa|capital=Tripoli}}.
# {{label|en|historical}} [[Africa]]; that is, the part of North Africa known in classical antiquity.

