Page 681 Australasia: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Australásia}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|Australasie}}, {{coin|en|Charles de Brosses|in=1756|nat=French|occ=scholar and politician|nobycat=1|nocap=1}}, from the {{der|en|la|-}} for “south of [[Asia]]”.<ref>{{R:Etymonline|accessdate=January 20, 2021}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɒstɹ(ə)lˈeɪʒə/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Australasia.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɔstɹl̩ˈæɪʒɐ/|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʒə|s=4}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# [[Oceania]].
# [[Australia]], [[New Zealand]], [[New Guinea]] and neighbouring [[island]]s.
#: {{holonyms|en|Oceania}}

====Usage notes====
This is an ambiguous term, whose precise meaning varies considerably depending on its field of use. It has been used interchangeably with the word [[Oceania]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|Australasian|pos=adj}}

