Page 757 Oceania: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Oceânia|Óceánia|Oceanía}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Oceanias Regions.png|thumb|Regions within Oceania.]]

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|Océanie}}, coined circa 1812 by geographer {{w|Conrad Malte-Brun}}, from the {{der|en|grc|Ὠκεανός||Oceanus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌəʊ.ʃiˈɑː.nɪə/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌoʊ.ʃiˈæn.i.ə/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɐʉ.ʃiːˈaː.ni.ə/|/-njə/|a=NZ}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌəʉ.ʃiˈaː.ni.ə/|/-njə/|a=Aus}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌoʊʃiˈænə/|a=IE,also}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Oceania.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|O|ce|a|nia}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q538}}{{place|en|geographical region/and/continent|composed of many islands ([[Melanesia]], [[Micronesia]], and [[Polynesia]]) plus [[Australasia]], located between [[Asia]], [[Antarctica]] and [[the Americas]]|tcl=a <<geographical region>> and <<continent>> composed of [[Australia]], [[New Zealand]] and the islands of [[Melanesia]], [[Micronesia]] and [[Polynesia]]}}.

====Usage notes====
Despite the fact that Oceania is not widely classified a continent in anglophone countries, some people use the term when referring to the continents of the world in place of the Australian continent, mostly because several Oceanian countries are located in the Pacific Ocean and would otherwise be unable to be classified within a continent unless grouped in with Australia.

Oceania contains the following countries:
{{top2}}
* [[Australia]]
* [[East Timor]] (sometimes included)
* [[Federated States of Micronesia]]
* [[Fiji]]
* [[Indonesia]] (part)
* [[Kiribati]]
* [[Marshall Islands]]
* [[Nauru]]
* [[New Zealand]]
* [[Palau]]
* [[Papua New Guinea]]
* [[Samoa]]
* [[Solomon Islands]]
* [[Tonga]]
* [[Tuvalu]]
* [[Vanuatu]]
{{bottom}}
Territories in Oceania belonging to other countries include:
{{top2}}
* [[Hawaii]] ([[United States]])
* [[American Samoa]] ([[United States]])
* [[Easter Island]] ([[Chile]])
* [[French Polynesia]] ([[France]])
* [[Bonin Islands]] ([[Japan]])
* [[Guam]] (United States)
* [[Wallis and Futuna]] (France)
* [[Northern Mariana Islands]] (United States)
* [[New Caledonia]] (France)
{{bottom}}

====Meronyms====
* {{l|en|Australasia}}
* {{l|en|Melanesia}}
* {{l|en|Micronesia}}
* {{l|en|Polynesia}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|Oceanic}}
* {{l|en|Oceanian}}
* {{l|en|Oceanianist}}
* {{l|en|ocean}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ja|bor=1|オセアニア|tr=Oseania}}

